section__
  @title "T265 - ACT4 - Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-265.jpg"

  "Wind knifes across Pyke bridge and turns sea spray into cold grit on your face as Yara Greyjoy presents a roster of ships available for hire. Balon studies you from behind driftwood pillars, saying nothing while captains shout over one another about targets, shares, and hostages. Your Essosi contracts bought grain and escorts; now the question is whether those lifelines survive the Ironborn appetite for plunder.

Neutrality is over. If your sea lanes are not protected by force, they are invitations. Yet force has a price structure of its own: each concession to raider custom teaches your allies that Valehart tolerates maritime extortion when convenient. Public terms can impose accountability on brutal men. Hidden terms can deliver faster obedience and leave a deeper rot.

Kelp, tar, and wet wool fill the bridge. You are not choosing whether to engage the islands. You are choosing how much of their logic you are willing to import into your rule."

  choice__
    @target "T266 - ACT4 - Dragonstone Blood Price at first light"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Set raiding limits and escort duties before sworn captains, accepting slower consensus to secure enforceable sea discipline"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T267 - ACT4 - Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Issue private letters of marque to favored crews, buying immediate control while hiding coercive concessions"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T268 - ACT4 - The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
    @when ((wealth + essos_ties + dragon_factor) >= 7)
    @action essos_ties = clampStat(essos_ties + 1, 0, 30)
    @action dragon_factor = clampStat(dragon_factor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Pay for foreign hulls and dragon-linked scouting, externalizing maritime pressure before Ironborn terms harden"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T266 - ACT4 - Dragonstone Blood Price at first light"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-266.jpg"

  "In a smoke-black longhall, Theon calls for negotiated shares while Victarion demands blood payment for two ships lost guarding your grain convoy. Thralls keep their eyes down as arguments sharpen into hand-on-axe silence. If the captains walk out split, your logistics net tears along faction lines before the next tide.

This is command coherence under raider law. A public compensation formula could keep crews predictable and give you paper to enforce later. A private intimidation campaign could bind dissenting captains overnight, but fear contracts must be renewed with fresh examples. You can also bypass the dispute with outside hulls, though every imported deckhand is an insult to island pride.

Hemp smoke stings your throat while tally stones click on a war table. What you pay at first light determines whether Ironborn service feels like alliance or occupation."

  choice__
    @target "T267 - ACT4 - Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Adopt a witnessed blood-price schedule for lost hulls, paying openly to preserve predictable chain of command"
