section__
  @title "T267 - ACT4 - Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-267.jpg"

  "At the saltwife market, shipwright clans present contracts stamped with lion wax taken from captured Blackwater couriers. Victarion wants to honor them as spoils law. Theon warns those seals are bait, and any public adoption ties Valehart to stolen legitimacy. Meanwhile two hostage families wait under guard, each convinced your signature will decide who drowns at dusk.

Delay is lethal here. Public adjudication can keep your reputation aligned with process even when outcomes hurt. Covert manipulation can free preferred hostages and secure faster compliance, but once clans discover edited terms, they will assume every future bargain is similarly trapped. The Iron Islands remember humiliation longer than debt.

Fish scales glitter in torchlight like coins on black cloth. This bargain is not just about Blackwater seals. It is about whether your maritime law is real or theatrical."

  choice__
    @target "T268 - ACT4 - The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
