section__
  @title "T270 - ACT4 - Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-270.jpg"

  "Fog from the eastern lanes hides three returning hulls and one missing flagship, and suddenly every captain on Pyke has a theory about who sold your route to Pentos raiders. Theon urges immediate public inquiry to keep crews from turning on each other. Victarion proposes retaliatory strikes tonight, before fear calcifies into mutiny.

You need discipline without paralysis. A visible convoy code can reduce panic and reassure merchants that Valehart still commands its own fleet. Secret reprisals may restore deterrence faster, but they also make casualty accounting unverifiable, feeding the same rumor economy that caused this crisis. If coin holds, you can hire outside force and compress the timeline at the cost of dependence.

Fog beads on your gloves while lookouts ring warning bells from the sea tower. Every bell asks the same question: will your response build order or simply spread terror."

