section__
  @title "T271 - ACT4 - Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-271.jpg"

  "Qartheen factors financing your island convoys split into rival blocs overnight, each accusing the other of feeding prices to your enemies. Victarion wants one bloc purged and its collateral seized. Theon argues that forcing both sides into a visible settlement keeps coin flowing and avoids another blood feud layered onto your naval crisis.

No captain will wait for perfect certainty. If you broker terms publicly, you preserve a framework that neutral crews can still trust. If you back one bloc in secret, you gain leverage and immediate liquidity while ensuring the losing side funds retaliation through every port it can reach. This is alliance maintenance under open predation.

Wet rope hangs from beams and drips onto loan tablets. What looks like a financing dispute is really a referendum on whether Valehart can keep partners aligned without permanent coercion."

