section__
  @title "T272 - ACT4 - The Wall War Map against old law"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-272.jpg"

  "A courier from the Wall arrives mud-streaked and exhausted, carrying a map that marks collapsing frontier depots and requests immediate sea transport for oil, iron, and grain. Balon calls the request a northern problem and wants those hulls reserved for richer raids. Yara says ignoring the frontier now buys a harder war later when panic reaches every port.

Desertion rumors have already spread through your mixed crews. A public commitment to Watch support can reinforce your image as a ruler with strategic horizon beyond plunder. A covert diversion of supplies to preferred raider fleets keeps tactical momentum but signals that existential threats are negotiable if profit is high enough. Once that signal is sent, it is hard to retract.

Cold rain starts over the market roofs while shipwrights wait for your loading orders. The map from the Wall is thin parchment, but the decision it demands is heavy."

  choice__
