section__
  @title "T273 - ACT4 - Castle Black Inheritance Claim under moonless sky"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-273.jpg"

  "A northern claimant arrives on Pyke under truce flag, carrying papers that transfer rights over captured Castle Black stores if Valehart recognizes his inheritance claim. Yara sees a lawful route to stable resupply. Balon sees an outsider trying to buy Ironborn policy with ink and old seals. Around them, raider captains ask only whether accepting the claim pays in grain, steel, or hostages.

Hostage pressure tightens by the hour. If you honor the claim in public hearing, you gain a defensible chain of title and risk immediate backlash from crews who expected plunder without constraints. If you crush the claimant quietly and redistribute the stores, discipline might hold through the week, but every northern ally will mark Valehart signatures as conditional theater.

Rain taps the tower shutters while clerks hold quills over wet parchment. This ruling determines whether your logistics run on recognisable law or on whichever blade is nearest."

  choice__
