  "A whispered warning from Moat Cailin reaches you by smugglers' skiff: causeway patrols have been bribed to misdirect your northbound cargo into raider waters. Theon argues for immediate public route changes before panic spreads. Victarion prefers to leak false routes and slaughter whoever takes the bait, then present the bodies as deterrence.

Information drift is now a tactical weapon. A transparent correction can reestablish command coherence and reassure nervous allies that Valehart still controls its routes. A covert trap might destroy your immediate enemies but confirms every rumor that your orders are a game of hidden knives. Either approach consumes scarce time on a clock already running short.

Coal smoke from tide braziers mixes with kelp stink on the dock. One set of route orders goes out tonight, and every captain will treat it as the new standard."

