section__
  @title "T275 - ACT4 - Oldtown Silent Betrayal behind closed doors"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-275.jpg"

  "A sealed packet from Oldtown reveals that one of your own chartmasters sold harbor depth tables to rival captains for a chest of silver and safe passage papers. Victarion demands immediate execution on the bridge as a lesson. Theon warns that summary violence will satisfy the crowd and leave the spy network intact.

Quartermasters already ration by loyalty, and this betrayal gives every underfed crew a story about favoritism. A public tribunal can surface accomplices and keep your command language legible. A hidden sweep can seize suspects before they run, but once men disappear without record, your own officers will begin writing contingencies against you.

Spray lashes the railing while the accused kneels with shackled wrists, staring at your banner instead of your face. How you punish betrayal here will define the discipline culture of every ship still under Valehart colors."

