  "Reach envoys offer bounty contracts for raids that cripple Highgarden's rivals, with payment in grain and sailcloth your fleet desperately needs. Yara wants the contracts formalized so captains know exactly which targets are lawful. Balon prefers ambiguous language that lets crews harvest whatever they can seize under the same banner.

Neutral captains are watching for one thing: whether Valehart policy protects them from retaliatory justice after the money is spent. A public target doctrine can preserve coalition coherence even if payouts shrink. A covert interpretation regime can maximize short-term extraction while guaranteeing future diplomatic blowback when burned villages start naming your signet in testimony.

Rust flakes from anchor chains onto the contract table like brown snow. This promise to Highgarden is really a decision about the legal shape of sanctioned violence."

  choice__
