section__
  @title "T278 - ACT4 - Sunspear Prison Confession with steel drawn"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-278.jpg"

  "A prisoner taken off Sunspear trade lanes confesses that several of your escort captains were paid to delay response during recent ambushes. Theon argues for open confrontation and immediate reassignment of command. Victarion says hesitation will look weak and pushes for quiet executions before dawn.

Desertion is already feeding on uncertainty. Public process could restore clarity and reassure loyal crews that advancement is not tied to hidden patrons. Secret punishments may stop current leaks faster, but they also create a fleet culture where everyone assumes accusations are political tools. You can retain speed with covert force, or retain legitimacy with slower proof, not both at once.

The prisoner trembles in chain shadow while gulls cry over the surf. Your decision tells every captain whether truth in Valehart service is documented, purchased, or feared."

  choice__
    @target "T279 - ACT4 - The Trident Salt Pact by the harbor chain"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Confront implicated captains in open muster, accepting disruption to reassert lawful and legible command standards"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T280 - ACT4 - Riverrun Broken Oath under rain"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 7)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Extract names in secret and purge quietly, restoring short-term control while corroding trust in due process"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T279 - ACT4 - The Trident Salt Pact by the harbor chain"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-279.jpg"

  "At the chain harbor, priests and captains gather to codify a Trident salt pact meant to stop indiscriminate raiding of allied grain routes. Victarion demands broad exemptions for prize-taking. Theon insists exemptions are exactly how every previous pact collapsed. Behind them, hostage kin line the quay and count how many clauses might keep their families alive.

If you sign strict public terms, you may protect strategic corridors and reduce revenge cycles that bleed your manpower. If you keep loopholes in private codicils, captains stay happy now and coalition partners prepare lawsuits, sanctions, and retaliatory strikes. The pact is not ceremonial; it is the operating system for your fleet as winter closes.

Salt wind snaps the banners while clerks hold molten wax over waiting seals. Whatever language you choose here will be quoted in every port court and every tavern brawl."

  choice__
    @target "T280 - ACT4 - Riverrun Broken Oath under rain"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Seal a strict public Trident salt pact, limiting opportunistic plunder to protect long-term coalition durability"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T281 - ACT4 - The Kingsroad Blackmail Ledger after the feast"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Embed private exemptions for favored crews, preserving short-term loyalty while inviting strategic retaliation"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T280 - ACT4 - Riverrun Broken Oath under rain"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-280.jpg"

  "A storm breaks over Pyke as ravens confirm a Riverrun oath partner has defaulted on promised harbor fees and hired raiders to cover the shortfall. Balon calls for immediate punitive seizure and public hanging. Yara warns that indiscriminate retaliation will collapse the fragile pact network you spent this act building.

Information edits spread faster than truth in bad weather. A documented legal response could hold your wider coalition together even if the culprit escapes the first strike. A covert extraction and reprisal might deliver swift justice, but it also writes another chapter in the same hidden-war playbook that keeps generating these crises. You can trade speed for legitimacy, or legitimacy for speed.

Rain rattles on shields stacked by the bridge and turns torch smoke into greasy streaks. This ruling closes the middle movement of Act 4 and determines what kind of fleet enters the next escalation."

  choice__
    @target "T281 - ACT4 - The Kingsroad Blackmail Ledger after the feast"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Answer the Riverrun breach through formal maritime censure and witness-backed penalties, preserving systemic legitimacy"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T282 - ACT4 - The Red Keep Raven Intercept before the sept bell"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 5)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Settle the breach through covert seizure and deniable reprisal, restoring tempo while deepening shadow-governance costs"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T283 - ACT4 - Winterfell Night Council before witnesses"
    @when ((wealth + essos_ties + dragon_factor) >= 7)
    @action essos_ties = clampStat(essos_ties + 1, 0, 30)
    @action dragon_factor = clampStat(dragon_factor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Fund outside enforcement flotillas to execute penalties fast, externalizing coercion at long-term strategic expense"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T281 - ACT4 - The Kingsroad Blackmail Ledger after the feast"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-281.jpg"

  "The reaver quartermasters lay out a blackmail ledger proving at least five captains have been billing Valehart for escorts they never sailed. Yara wants names read aloud before the full hall and restitution seized in daylight. Balon warns that humiliating veteran raiders publicly could fracture the fleet when you still need every hull.

Rations are already short, and false accounting turns scarcity into mutiny fuel. A public correction campaign could restore enough trust for orderly provisioning. A secret arrangement with the worst offenders might keep ships in line through intimidation, but it teaches every crew that fraud is negotiable if your knives are sharp enough. The ledger is numbers, but the consequences are political memory.

Hemp smoke clings to your cloak while thralls watch for the first captain named. This is a decision about whether discipline here is written, whispered, or bought."

  choice__
    @target "T282 - ACT4 - The Red Keep Raven Intercept before the sept bell"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Read the fraud ledger before assembled crews and enforce visible penalties, sacrificing speed to rebuild command legitimacy"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T283 - ACT4 - Winterfell Night Council before witnesses"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Cut private immunity deals with key offenders, preserving short-term cohesion while normalizing hidden corruption"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T282 - ACT4 - The Red Keep Raven Intercept before the sept bell"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-282.jpg"

  "Intercepted raven packets from King's Landing describe your island policy as indistinguishable from piracy-for-hire and invite rival houses to outbid you for Ironborn service. Theon insists you counter publicly before the accusation hardens into shared truth. Victarion says truth never mattered on these waters and pushes for retaliatory seizures against any ship carrying crown correspondence.

One choice prioritizes narrative legitimacy, the other deterrence through fear. Public correction could preserve ties with cautious allies and keep neutral ports open. Covert retaliation can disrupt enemy planning quickly, but once mail ships start vanishing, every court blames Valehart first and asks questions later. Communication warfare is now as material as grain.

Rust and fish oil stain the message table while scribes compare wax seals for forgery. Your response here determines whether people trust your words or only your reach."

  choice__
    @target "T283 - ACT4 - Winterfell Night Council before witnesses"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Issue a public counter-dispatch with verifiable ledgers and witnesses, accepting short-term embarrassment to restore trust"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T284 - ACT4 - The Twins Debt Collection under wolf banners"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 7)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Disrupt hostile raven traffic through covert captures and bribes, regaining initiative while escalating deniable war"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T283 - ACT4 - Winterfell Night Council before witnesses"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-283.jpg"

  "Winterfell's night council sends hard terms: if Ironborn raids keep touching northern grain, your alliance is suspended regardless of promises already paid for. Victarion calls the warning predictable posturing. Theon points out that northern withdrawal would strand half your logistics on hostile coasts and turn every current pact into scrap.

There is no neutral lane left. A public recommitment to northern protection can stabilize allied planning and reduce retaliatory spirals. A private coercion strategy against troublesome captains may keep raid tempo high while pretending compliance, but once exposed it will confirm every northern fear about Valehart double-dealing. The cost of duplicity rises each time you use it.

Sea wind whistles through arrow slits as your messengers wait for sealed orders. This reply decides whether the North sees a partner or a temporary necessity."

  choice__
    @target "T284 - ACT4 - The Twins Debt Collection under wolf banners"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Reaffirm northern protections in witnessed council terms, spending leverage now to preserve alliance credibility"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T285 - ACT4 - Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Force compliance through private threats to raider chiefs, holding tempo while eroding trust with northern partners"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T284 - ACT4 - The Twins Debt Collection under wolf banners"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-284.jpg"

  "Agents from the Twins demand emergency toll settlements on every cargo that moved under your salt pact, citing clauses no one remembers signing. Balon wants the collectors drowned as extortionists. Yara argues that some claims are valid and denying all of them turns your fleet into declared debtors in half the river ports.

Desertion reports worsen whenever wages look uncertain. A public debt audit could separate predatory claims from legitimate ones and keep your treasury math believable. A covert payoff-and-threat strategy can silence claimants faster, but it commits Valehart to permanent off-book spending and emboldens every future extortionist who thinks you'll pay to avoid scrutiny.

Water slaps stone pilings beneath the dock while toll sheets flap in wet wind. Tonight you choose whether debt pressure is resolved in law, in fear, or in expensive ambiguity."

  choice__
    @target "T285 - ACT4 - Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Audit and settle Twins claims through open accounting, accepting friction now to protect long-term fiscal legitimacy"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T286 - ACT4 - Dragonstone Blood Price at first light"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 5)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Handle claimants through covert payments and intimidation, restoring short-term calm while expanding hidden liabilities"
  __choice
