section__
  @title "T285 - ACT4 - Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-285.jpg"

  "A fresh census of hulls and crew strength reveals the hidden cost of weeks of coercive maritime politics: too many wounded oarsmen, too few trustworthy officers, and three captains holding hostages they were never authorized to take. Yara says the numbers demand consolidation and reduced raiding scope. Balon insists shrinking operations now invites every rival to test your weakness.

Hostage politics are no longer abstract; they are consuming manpower and legitimacy at the same time. A public consolidation order can preserve the fleet core for the next act. Secretly rewarding aggressive captains may keep outward momentum while locking you into a cycle where each success depends on one more unacceptable concession.

The bridge planks shudder beneath marching boots as clerks call out losses. Census figures do not care about pride, only sustainability."

