section__
  @title "T286 - ACT4 - Dragonstone Blood Price at first light"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-286.jpg"

  "Before dawn, watchers report smoke trails offshore and rumors that Dragonstone-aligned crews are offering protection contracts to the same ports you tax. Theon urges a public nonaggression framework to avoid fighting both rivals and weather. Victarion demands preemptive strikes to prove no dragon banner will dictate terms in Iron waters.

Raven edits and deliberate leaks have already blurred reality enough that overreaction is its own trap. A public deconfliction order can protect trade and buy clarity. Covert escalation through deniable raids may win immediate fear advantage and accelerate broader war with actors far stronger than your current fleet can absorb.

The longhall braziers spit resin as first light leaks under the doors. Whatever you declare at dawn becomes the baseline for how dragon power is treated in your maritime strategy."

  choice__
