section__
  @title "T287 - ACT4 - Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-287.jpg"

  "The final island bargain opens in a salt market turned war chancery, where lion-sealed brokers offer short-term fuel and bolts if you prioritize their convoys above northern and Watch obligations. Victarion wants the deal; he can enforce it with steel. Theon says choosing lion coin now will detonate the coalition architecture you have spent the act trying to stabilize.

This is an end-of-module pressure point: whichever side gets priority sets expectations for Act 4's final movement. A public balancing order can preserve multi-front viability at lower immediate profit. A covert preference structure can keep the fleet paid through next week while ensuring every excluded ally plans revenge. If treasury allows, outsourcing the gap buys time but reduces sovereign control.

Market gutters run with fish blood and rainwater while seals wait on hot wax. One signature decides who still believes your hierarchy of obligations."

