section__
  @title "T288 - ACT4 - The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-iron-islands/frame-288.jpg"

  "Crowded galleries on the sea tower roar as Balon demands one decisive northern strike to prove Ironborn primacy before dragon politics engulf the coast. Yara argues the fleet needs disciplined redeployment, not spectacle, if Valehart wants to survive the next phase. Your officers stare between them, waiting to see whether command this act ends in consolidation or escalation.

The ultimatum is simple and brutal: choose legible structure and preserve governability, or choose coercive acceleration and gamble that fear outpaces fatigue. A public, bounded order can carry credibility into the Targaryen arc. A covert push through intimidation can force movement now, but it does so with crews already stretched thin and suspicious of every sealed message.

Sea spray lashes the windows while horns call shift change below. This is the hinge between maritime coercion politics and dragon-era risk, and your final island decision will follow you into both."

  choice__
    @target "T289 - ACT4 - The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Issue a bounded public redeployment order, prioritizing coherent command over maximal short-term intimidation"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T290 - ACT4 - Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 5)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Drive a covert high-tempo strike plan through threats and deniable orders, maximizing pressure while compounding trust collapse"
  __choice
__section
